# Per-environment runtime settings applied to the Function App's App Settings
# (i.e. environment variables at runtime).
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the LIST OF KEYS.
#   - Only keys written here as `KEY=` are registered and applied
#   - Do not put values here; put them in .env.stg / .env.prod (gitignored)
#
# Usage:
#   1. Add the keys you need to this file as `KEY=` (leave the value empty)
#   2. cp .env.example .env.stg   # for stg (use .env.prod for prod)
#   3. Fill in the values in .env.stg and run `make setup-secrets`
#      → registered as Secrets in the matching GitHub Environment (stg / prod)
#   4. Run the Deploy workflow in GitHub Actions; the values are applied to the Function App's App Settings
#      → available in code as process.env.KEY
#
# Keys left empty are skipped; existing Secrets / App Settings are preserved.
#
# Example (a bot that calls an external API):
# EXTERNAL_API_URL=
# EXTERNAL_API_KEY=
